  "objectives": [
    { "id": "O1", "text": "Choosing the product-development track starts main0, the trio and the six specialists, each from an archetype file." },
    { "id": "O2", "text": "Bound agents nudge themselves with rlcd over a digest of keys, not a transcript, and never wake an LLM by default." },
    { "id": "O3", "text": "What one surface offers, every surface offers in its form; a gap is a finding in CI." }
  ],
  "stories": [
    { "id": "S1", "text": "thread start --track product-development (and the app and plugin choice) starts main0, the trio and the six specialists with their configs; agents check refuses a missing tool and reports an extra one. Variations: V1 unknown track (failure: refused with the known tracks); V2 a specialist archetype that names a tool the harness lacks (failure: agents check names it).", "objectives": ["O1"],
      "tests": ["test:crates/legionctl/tests/agents.rs::the_product_development_track_starts_main_the_trio_and_six_specialists_from_their_archetypes"] },
    { "id": "S2", "kind": "control-flow", "text": "A self-nudge is an rlcd question on a trigger over a digest; yes gives main0 a short note, no gives nothing. Variations: V1 digest over the model's context (success: the question is split or goes to the owner, never cut silently); V2 rlcd call fails (failure: the failed step is recorded, no note, no LLM wake in its place).", "objectives": ["O2"],
      "tests": ["test:crates/legionctl/tests/threads.rs::a_self_nudge_asks_rlcd_over_a_digest_and_notes_main_only_on_yes"] },
    { "id": "S3", "kind": "requirement", "text": "The coherence check lists each operation and seed view with the surfaces that offer it (CLI, MCP, TUI, app); a gap fails CI with its name. Variations: V1 an operation with no app action (failure: named).", "objectives": ["O3"],
      "tests": ["test:crates/legionctl/tests/e2e.rs::each_operation_and_view_is_offered_on_every_surface_or_named_as_a_gap"] }
  ],
